  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nType parameters named var, \\_, record or partial (#357, closes #319). A target or method type parameter with one of these names made the imposter fail to compile:\n\nvar and \\_ turned the generated locals and discards into the type parameter;\n\na generated declaration that starts with record or, from C# 14, partial read as a record or a partial member.\n\nSuch a type parameter now takes another name in generated code, one that no type parameter, parameter or member beside it uses. You still write the imposter and its setups with your own type arguments, as before.\n\nMaintenance\n\nGenerated code now passes in arguments with in in every place that forwards them (#352, closes #322), and the generator dropped some dead code and duplicated logic (#351, #353, #355). The generated imposters behave the same.",
